{"name":"Sunburnt Cyclops","hex":"#ff404c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sunburnt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a sunburn or dark tan; having been burned by the sun's rays.","Dried out by the sun's rays."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of sunburn"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunburnt"},{"term":"cyclops","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A one-eyed giant from Greek and Roman mythology.","A one-eyed creature of any species."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cyclops"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sunburnt","blocks":[{"text":"Sunburnt is an album by Martin Phillipps & the Chills, though more correctly by Martin Phillipps alone. Owing to visa problems, the usual Chills line-up were not able to take part in the recording sessions, and session musicians Dave Gregory and Dave Mattacks appeared on all tracks, with Phillipps handling vocal, keyboard, and guitar parts, as well as some of the percussion. Craig Leon, the album's producer, also appeared on several of the tracks."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/98/Sunburnt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunburnt"},{"title":"Cyclopes","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek mythology and later Roman mythology, the Cyclopes are giant one-eyed creatures. Three kinds of Cyclopes can be distinguished. In Hesiod's Theogony, the Cyclopes are three brothers—Brontes, Steropes, and Arges—who create Zeus's thunderbolt, Poseidon's trident, and Hades' Helm of Darkness. The Cyclopes of Homer's Odyssey are a group of uncivilized, cave-dwelling shepherds, including Polyphemus, whom Odysseus encounters. A third group of Cyclopes reputedly constructed the Cyclopean walls of Mycenae and Tiryns."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Head_of_a_Cyclops_Colosseum.jpg/330px-Head_of_a_Cyclops_Co